GRA-17 -- FM edge-array growth publishes the new size before reallocating
==========================================================================
kgraphMapFmEdgeResize did `edxxsiz *= 2; *edxxsizptr = edxxsiz;` BEFORE the
memRealloc, and its callers kgraphMapFmPartAdd/PartAdd2 ignored the return value.
On a reallocation failure the published size claims the larger array while the
buffer is unchanged, and the next slot is written past it.

The resize path is only reached under memory pressure (edxxsiz starts at 16x the
frontier, capped at edgenbr). To exercise it deterministically, an IDENTICAL
fault hook was added to the memRealloc call in both a pristine and a patched
SCOTCH_DEBUG_ALL libscotch (the only real difference being the GRA-17 fix):

  /* in kgraphMapFmEdgeResize, both libs */
  if ((edxxtmp = ((getenv ("GRA17_FAIL") != NULL) ? NULL
                  : memRealloc (edxxtab, edxxsiz * sizeof (KgraphMapFmEdge)))) == NULL) {

Then, with strategy
  m{vert=30,low=r{sep=h{pass=10}},asc=b{width=3,bnd=d{pass=40}f{bal=0.05,move=120},org=f{bal=0.05,move=120}}}
on a 40x40 grid onto cmplt(64):
  GRA17_FAIL=1 ./gra17_pristine 40 64 "$STRAT"
    -> ERROR: kgraphMapFmEdgeResize: out of memory
    -> AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow WRITE of size 4
         #0 kgraphMapFmPartAdd kgraph_map_fm.c:717
         #1 kgraphMapFm         kgraph_map_fm.c:1114
  GRA17_FAIL=1 ./gra17_patched 40 64 "$STRAT"
    -> FM returns the failure cleanly, no overflow in kgraphMapFm
       (a separate downstream mapTerm NULL-deref then appears -- recorded as
        PS2-G13-1 in extra.json; it is a graphMapCompute2 error-path weakness,
        not part of GRA-17).

failrealloc.c is an LD_PRELOAD realloc-fail shim kept for reference; it cannot be
used together with ASan (ASan's own realloc interceptor wins), which is why the
in-source hook above was used instead.

7.0.18 round (non-debug ASan trees; hook applied identically to a copy of $INFRA/asan (hookp) and of the
patched $WORK/build (hookq): the getenv hook above, plus the release-mode initial size forced to the debug one,
`edxxsiz = 2 * grafptr->fronnbr + 1;`, so that kgraphMapFmEdgeResize is reached without SCOTCH_DEBUG_KGRAPH2):
  GRA17_FAIL=1 ./gra17_hookp 40 64 "$STRAT"   (pristine 7.0.18, i.e. with upstream 25322c9a)
    -> 26 x "kgraphMapFmEdgeResize: out of memory / kgraphMapFmPartAdd: cannot resize", FM keeps going, then
       AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow READ ... _SCOTCHkgraphMapFm kgraph_map_fm.c:1606 (rc 1)
  GRA17_FAIL=1 ./gra17_hookq 40 64 "$STRAT"   (series)
    -> "kgraphMapFm: cannot add vertex (1)" / "kgraphMapMl2: cannot apply ascending strategy", then the
       mapTerm NULL load in graphMapCompute2 (PS2-G13-1, G05's item, still present in 7.0.18).
